4. Make Jump and Extra Attack Match the Other Action Buttons

Current issue

The Jump and Extra Attack buttons do not have the same appearance as the other circular action buttons.

In css/touch-controls.css, the general .tc-btn class already defines the standard button appearance.

However, separate CSS overrides change Jump and Extra Attack.

For example:

* .tc-extra_attack increases size to 112%, changes border width to 3px, and applies its own background and border colors.
* .tc-jump applies a different background and border color.

These differences make the action cluster visually inconsistent.

Required behavior

Jump and Extra Attack must use the exact same standard button design as the other action buttons.

Standardize:

* Diameter.
* Circular shape.
* Border thickness.
* Border color.
* Background color.
* Transparency.
* Shadow.
* Pressed animation.
* Pressed-state background and border.
* Default visual intensity.

Use the shared .tc-btn styling as the primary source of truth.

Remove unnecessary visual overrides rather than creating new overrides to imitate the other buttons.

Extra Attack

Remove its special enlarged appearance and oversized border.

Extra Attack should have the same outer diameter, border, background, and pressed feedback as Attack 1–5.

Keep:

* Its existing position in the action cluster.
* Its fighter-specific sprite preview.
* Its accessible name.
* Its existing gameplay behavior.

The fighter’s artwork may differ, but the button container must look identical.

Jump

Remove its special background and border styling.

Jump must use the same button appearance as the others.

Keep:

* Its upward-arrow symbol.
* Its existing position.
* Its standard and higher-jump mechanics.
* Its airborne jump functionality.
* Its existing touch handling.

Action cluster layout

Preserve the intended layout:

        [4]   [5]   [EXTRA]
     [3]   [TRANSFORM] [SHIELD]
        [1]   [2]   [JUMP]

All these action buttons should now have consistent outer dimensions.

Recalculate any cluster geometry that previously depended on Extra Attack being larger.

Do not introduce overlaps or uneven alignment.

Existing special visual states that communicate actual gameplay information, such as unavailable abilities or reserved Transform, should remain functional.

